WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.089
When a diagnosis takes years, every visit
sends its own bill.

00:00:04.089 --> 00:00:06.234
Nobody adds up the whole search.

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:09.227
Waypoint Ledger does, free, with no
account.

00:00:09.227 --> 00:00:12.832
Tell it the way you remember it, and leave
out names.

00:00:12.832 --> 00:00:15.428
Four lines. Twelve hundred and four
dollars,

00:00:15.428 --> 00:00:17.610
from Medicare's published 2026 rates.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.498
That's the floor, not your bill.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.199
Open any line: the federal file, the exact
row.

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:24.696
No model sets a price,

00:00:24.696 --> 00:00:27.691
and every figure reproduces from its
source.

00:00:27.691 --> 00:00:30.237
Pick your coverage. On Original Medicare,

00:00:30.237 --> 00:00:33.901
it splits the total into what Medicare
pays and your share.

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:38.031
For Medicare records, it connects through
the CMS Blue Button sandbox.

00:00:38.031 --> 00:00:40.686
This is a made-up test patient CMS
publishes.

00:00:40.686 --> 00:00:43.164
Real records need CMS production approval.

00:00:43.164 --> 00:00:47.083
The code and data are open, for any team
to run.

00:00:47.533 --> 00:00:51.732
But some of the cost never reaches a bill.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:57.114
We asked people about their own illness
which cost weighed most.

00:00:57.114 --> 00:01:00.281
The care they went without came out on
top.

00:01:00.281 --> 00:01:03.153
It was also named most often as the one

00:01:03.153 --> 00:01:05.584
no one had ever asked them about.

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:08.620
A test the doctor wouldn't order.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:11.332
Being told you didn't meet criteria.

00:01:11.332 --> 00:01:12.990
You can count it here.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:17.500
No federal cost file has a row for it, so
we never price it.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.186
Print one page for your next appointment,
every figure cited.

00:01:21.186 --> 00:01:24.608
What did your search cost? Find out at
waypointledger.org.
